null,"citationCount":23,"membership":{"source":"Crossref exact journal ISSN","status":"verified","confidence":1,"evidenceUrl":"https://api.crossref.org/journals/0269-2821/works?filter=from-pub-date%3A2024-01-01%2Cuntil-pub-date%3A2024-12-31%2Ctype%3Ajournal-article&rows=180&cursor=*&sort=published&order=desc&select=DOI%2Ctitle%2Cauthor%2Cpublished%2Cpublished-online%2Cpublished-print%2Cissued%2Cpage%2CISSN%2CURL%2Cabstract%2Cis-referenced-by-count%2Cvolume%2Cissue"},"venueId":"j-springer-air","eventYear":2024,"topics":[],"methodTags":["prototype or system"],"classificationEvidence":"title-only"},{"id":"crossref:10.1007/s10462-023-10622-0","crossrefId":"10.1007/s10462-023-10622-0","editionId":"j-springer-air-2024","proceedingsKey":"journal:02692821:2024","title":"Interpretable scientific discovery with symbolic regression: a review","authors":[{"position":1,"name":"Nour Makke","orcid":null,"dblpPid":null},{"position":2,"name":"Sanjay Chawla","orcid":null,"dblpPid":null}],"publicationYear":2024,"pages":null,"doi":"10.1007/s10462-023-10622-0","publisherUrl":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10462-023-10622-0","dblpUrl":null,"openAccessUrl":null,"abstract":"Abstract Symbolic regression is emerging as a promising machine learning method for learning succinct underlying interpretable mathematical expressions directly from data. Whereas it has been traditionally tackled with genetic programming, it has recently gained a growing interest in deep learning as a data-driven model discovery tool, achieving significant advances in various application domains ranging from fundamental to applied sciences. In this survey, we present a structured and comprehensive overview of symbolic regression methods, review the adoption of these methods for model discovery in various areas, and assess their effectiveness. We have also grouped state-of-the-art symbolic regression applications in a categorized manner in a living review.","citationCount":277,"membership":{"source":"Crossref exact journal ISSN","status":"verified","confidence":1,"evidenceUrl":"https://api.crossref.org/journals/0269-2821/works?filter=from-pub-date%3A2024-01-01%2Cuntil-pub-date%3A2024-12-31%2Ctype%3Ajournal-article&rows=180&cursor=*&sort=published&order=desc&select=DOI%2Ctitle%2Cauthor%2Cpublished%2Cpublished-online%2Cpublished-print%2Cissued%2Cpage%2CISSN%2CURL%2Cabstract%2Cis-referenced-by-count%2Cvolume%2Cissue"},"venueId":"j-springer-air","eventYear":2024,"topics":["AI & machine learning"],"methodTags":["survey or review","deep learning","prototype or system"],"classificationEvidence":"title-and-abstract"},{"id":"crossref:10.1007/s10462-023-10636-8","crossrefId":"10.1007/s10462-023-10636-8","editionId":"j-springer-air-2024","proceedingsKey":"journal:02692821:2024","title":"State-of-the-art review of machine learning and optimization algorithms applications in environmental effects of blasting","authors":[{"position":1,"name":"Jian Zhou","orcid":null,"dblpPid":null},{"position":2,"name":"Yulin Zhang","orcid":null,"dblpPid":null},{"position":3,"name":"Yingui Qiu","orcid":null,"dblpPid":null}],"publicationYear":2024,"pages":null,"doi":"10.1007/s10462-023-10636-8","publisherUrl":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10462-023-10636-8","dblpUrl":null,"openAccessUrl":null,"abstract":null,"citationCount":56,"membership":{"source":"Crossref exact journal ISSN","status":"verified","confidence":1,"evidenceUrl":"https://api.crossref.org/journals/0269-2821/works?filter=from-pub-date%3A2024-01-01%2Cuntil-pub-date%3A2024-12-31%2Ctype%3Ajournal-article&rows=180&cursor=*&sort=published&order=desc&select=DOI%2Ctitle%2Cauthor%2Cpublished%2Cpublished-online%2Cpublished-print%2Cissued%2Cpage%2CISSN%2CURL%2Cabstract%2Cis-referenced-by-count%2Cvolume%2Cissue"},"venueId":"j-springer-air","eventYear":2024,"topics":["AI & machine learning"],"methodTags":["prototype or system"],"classificationEvidence":"title-only"},{"id":"crossref:10.1007/s10462-023-10637-7","crossrefId":"10.1007/s10462-023-10637-7","editionId":"j-springer-air-2024","proceedingsKey":"journal:02692821:2024","title":"The key artificial intelligence technologies in early childhood education: a review","authors":[{"position":1,"name":"Honghu Yi","orcid":null,"dblpPid":null},{"position":2,"name":"Ting Liu","orcid":"0000-0002-8208-3430","dblpPid":null},{"position":3,"name":"Gongjin Lan","orcid":"0000-0003-2020-8186","dblpPid":null}],"publicationYear":2024,"pages":null,"doi":"10.1007/s10462-023-10637-7","publisherUrl":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10462-023-10637-7","dblpUrl":null,"openAccessUrl":null,"abstract":null,"citationCount":60,"membership":{"source":"Crossref exact journal ISSN","status":"verified","confidence":1,"evidenceUrl":"https://api.crossref.org/journals/0269-2821/works?filter=from-pub-date%3A2024-01-01%2Cuntil-pub-date%3A2024-12-31%2Ctype%3Ajournal-article&rows=180&cursor=*&sort=published&order=desc&select=DOI%2Ctitle%2Cauthor%2Cpublished%2Cpublished-online%2Cpublished-print%2Cissued%2Cpage%2CISSN%2CURL%2Cabstract%2Cis-referenced-by-count%2Cvolume%2Cissue"},"venueId":"j-springer-air","eventYear":2024,"topics":["AI & machine learning","education & learning"],"methodTags":[],"classificationEvidence":"title-only"},{"id":"crossref:10.1007/s10462-023-10629-7","crossrefId":"10.1007/s10462-023-10629-7","editionId":"j-springer-air-2024","proceedingsKey":"journal:02692821:2024","title":"Understanding rate of return dynamics of cryptocurrencies: an experimental campaign","authors":[{"position":1,"name":"Krzysztof Koszewski","orcid":null,"dblpPid":null},{"position":2,"name":"Somnath Mazumdar","orcid":null,"dblpPid":null},{"position":3,"name":"Anoop S. Kumar","orcid":null,"dblpPid":null}],"publicationYear":2024,"pages":null,"doi":"10.1007/s10462-023-10629-7","publisherUrl":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10462-023-10629-7","dblpUrl":null,"openAccessUrl":null,"abstract":"Abstract In recent years, cryptocurrencies have been considered as an asset by public investors and received much research attention. It is a volatile asset, thus predicting its prices is not easy due to the dependence on multiple external factors. Machine learning models are becoming popular for cryptocurrency price predictions, while also considering social media data. In this article, we analyze the rate of return of three cryptocurrencies (Bitcoin, Ether, Binance) from an investor point of view. We also consider three traditional external variables: S&amp;P 500 stock market index, gold price, and volatility index. The rate of return prediction is based on three stages. First, we analyze the correlation between the cryptocurrency returns and the traditional external variables. Next, we focus on the influential social media variables (from Twitter, Reddit, and Wikipedia). Later, we use these variables to improve prediction accuracy. Third, we test how the standard time series models (such as ARIMA and SARIMA) and four machine learning models (such as RNN, LSTM, GRU and Bi-LSTM) predict one-day rate of return. Finally, we also analyze the risk of investing in each cryptocurrencies using value risk statistics. Overall, our result shows no correlation between cryptocurrency returns and three traditional external variables. Second, we found that overall LSTM model is the best, GRU is the second-best prediction model, while the impact of the social media variables varies depending on the cryptocurrencies. Finally, we also found that investment in gold offers better returns than cryptocurrency during Covid-19-like situations.","citationCount":3,"membership":{"source":"Crossref exact journal ISSN","status":"verified","confidence":1,"evidenceUrl":"https://api.crossref.org/journals/0269-2821/works?filter=from-pub-date%3A2024-01-01%2Cuntil-pub-date%3A2024-12-31%2Ctype%3Ajournal-article&rows=180&cursor=*&sort=published&order=desc&select=DOI%2Ctitle%2Cauthor%2Cpublished%2Cpublished-online%2Cpublished-print%2Cissued%2Cpage%2CISSN%2CURL%2Cabstract%2Cis-referenced-by-count%2Cvolume%2Cissue"},"venueId":"j-springer-air","eventYear":2024,"topics":["AI & machine learning","sustainability & society"],"methodTags":["controlled experiment"],"classificationEvidence":"title-and-abstract"}],"insights":{"venueId":"j-springer-air","startYear":2024,"endYear":2024,"paperCount":14,"themes":[{"label":"AI & machine learning","count":8},{"label":"computer vision","count":2},{"label":"sustainability & society","count":2},{"label":"education & learning","count":1},{"label":"health & assistive technology","count":1}],"methods":[{"label":"prototype or system","count":8},{"label":"deep learning","count":5},{"label":"survey or review","count":4},{"label":"controlled experiment","count":2},{"label":"case study","count":1}],"extractionEvidence":"title-and-abstract","generatedAt":"2026-08-02T21:44:44.463Z"}}
